The kernels (energy loss, electron ionisation, multiple scattering, bremsstrahlung, annihilation, muon radiative
losses, slab propagation, GDML world ray tracing, transport, crossings, annulus geometry, helix stepping, precision
and determinism settings, materials) and their tests were extracted from mu2e-fastsim (commit 2d332489) and made
experiment-neutral: the Mu2e geometry's materials, field-map scale and GPU launch settings stay in mu2e-fastsim,
which installs them through hepsimkernels.materials.register, ehelix.MAP_SCALE and precision.PROVENANCE_HOOKS.
The tests register the public Mu2e GDML materials as an example experiment's materials (tests/example_materials.py).

The bundled tables are compact copies of Geant4 data: data/brem_sb_G4EMLOW8.6.1.npz (G4EMLOW 8.6.1 brem_SB, the
Seltzer-Berger bremsstrahlung cross sections) and data/mott_G4MottData_11.3.2.npz (the Mott/Rutherford fit coefficients of
Geant4 11.3.2's G4MottData.hh, used by G4ScreeningMottCrossSection). Geant4 and its data are distributed under the Geant4 Software License
(https://geant4.web.cern.ch/license); each table's manifest records its source files and their SHA-256.
